[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Understanding Browser Contexts and Isolation in Playwright"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Playwright introduces the concept of Browser Contexts to handle test isolation efficiently. A browser context acts as an isolated incognito-like session within a single browser instance, ensuring complete separation of cookies, local storage, and cache."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"What is a Browser Context?"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"In traditional automation tools, achieving session isolation often meant launching a completely new browser instance for each test, which is resource-intensive. Playwright optimizes this by launching a single browser process and creating multiple independent browser contexts within it."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Each browser context has its own independent cookie store."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"LocalStorage and SessionStorage do not leak between contexts."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Permissions and geolocation can be configured per context."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Code Example: Creating Isolated Contexts"},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"const { chromium } = require('playwright');

(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();

  // Create first independent context
  const contextOne = await browser.newContext();
  const pageOne = await contextOne.newPage();
  await pageOne.goto('https://example.com');

  // Create second independent context
  const contextTwo = await browser.newContext();
  const pageTwo = await contextTwo.newPage();
  await pageTwo.goto('https://example.com');

  await browser.close();
})();"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Handling Multiple Users in a Single Test"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Browser contexts are extremely useful for testing collaborative features, such as chat applications or admin-versus-user workflows. You can easily simulate two different logged-in users simultaneously within the same test script."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"// Admin context
const adminContext = await browser.newContext();
const adminPage = await adminContext.newPage();

// Regular user context
const userContext = await browser.newContext();
const userPage = await userContext.newPage();"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Leveraging Playwright browser contexts reduces execution time while maintaining strict test isolation. By avoiding the overhead of launching multiple browser binaries, your test suites run faster and more reliably."}]
